WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.569
-Hello and welcome back
to our makeshift studio

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:04.937
in an attic crawl space.

00:00:04.937 --> 00:00:08.608
So far, we've migrated
from the hallway to the garage

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:10.543
to the living room to the attic.

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.278
And you may be wondering

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:13.980
what's that little door
behind me?

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.782
Is it where we keep
our camping gear?

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.316
Or is it a door
to another dimension?

00:00:17.316 --> 00:00:19.786
And how about that tiny chair?

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:20.920
Is it for my kids,

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.856
or is that where
the attic hobbit smokes his pipe

00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:25.791
and reminisces about
the Battle of the Five Armies?

00:00:25.791 --> 00:00:28.327
I'm sorry to say
I'll never tell.

00:00:28.327 --> 00:00:30.763
Now, we're all bracing for
a very difficult few weeks --

00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:33.132
or months, but there are things
the federal government

00:00:33.132 --> 00:00:35.234
could be doing right now
to help us get through this.

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:37.771
Instead, the president
has essentially

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:39.739
abdicated his responsibility

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:41.441
and left the states
up to themselves.

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:44.110
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:47.980 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:51.517
A pandemic like this requires
a centralized federal Response.

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:54.053
You know how Republicans always
complain about big government?

00:00:54.053 --> 00:00:57.456
Well, how sweet would
a big government be right now?

00:00:57.456 --> 00:00:59.225
Because I don't know about you,

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:01.260
but this tiny government stuff
sucks.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:03.663
It's like being on the top floor
of a burning building,

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.664
but instead of a catch net,
the firemen show up

00:01:05.664 --> 00:01:08.200
with a little workout
trampoline.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:09.435
Feels like right now

00:01:09.435 --> 00:01:11.670
we've largely been left
to fend for ourselves.

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:14.941
For example, for weeks we were
told that masks don't work

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:16.276
and that we shouldn't wear them.

00:01:16.276 --> 00:01:18.778
Now all of a sudden, the CDC
is considering

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:21.047
recommending mask usage
for all Americans.

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:23.316
You might want answers about
what you should be doing

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:24.517
to protect yourself and others

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:27.086
and why the government
is changing its position.

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:30.223
Instead, the best advice the
president could offer on Tuesday

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:31.991
was this --

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:33.692
-You know, you can use a scarf.

00:01:33.692 --> 00:01:36.629
A scarf is -- everybody --
a lot of people have scarves.

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:39.198
And you can use a scarf.
A scarf would be very good.

00:01:39.198 --> 00:01:41.834
I would say do it.
But use a scarf if you want.

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:44.970
I mean, most people have scarves
and scarves are very good.

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:47.740
-Oh, great. So now the president
is Martha Stewart.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.475
[ As Trump ] Using a blanket,
a bike helmet,

00:01:49.475 --> 00:01:53.412
and some Saran wrap, you can
make your own hazmat suit.

00:01:53.412 --> 00:01:55.147
Homemade. Pretty great.

00:01:55.147 --> 00:01:57.784
[ Normal voice ] But it's true.
Most people do have scarves

00:01:57.784 --> 00:02:00.619
and no one has more scarves
than Lenny Kravitz.

00:02:00.619 --> 00:02:04.056
So breathe easy, everyone.
Lenny Kravitz is in the clear.

00:02:04.056 --> 00:02:06.659
I mean, obviously the man
has been preparing

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:08.727
for this moment his entire life.
I mean, look at that.

00:02:08.727 --> 00:02:10.430
Not only can he use that scarf,

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:12.065
he can share it with
two other people

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:15.001
while maintaining
a six-foot difference.

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:17.837
Now, it's true, there is
evidence that wearing a mask

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.472
or some other kind of face
covering,

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.107
even something rudimentary,

00:02:21.107 --> 00:02:24.310
can prevent asymptomatic spread
of the disease.

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:26.279
You can wear a bandanna.
You can wear a cloth.

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:28.547
Just don't be a guy
who wears a Jason mask.

00:02:28.547 --> 00:02:30.750
I mean, one, it's freaky,
and two, it literally has holes.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:35.521
Jason, come on, man, that mask
is not approved by the CDC.

00:02:35.521 --> 00:02:38.591
Haven't you killed
enough people, Jason?

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:42.462
Now, the president could have
gone into detail about that

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:44.797
or any other number
of other important issues

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:46.799
during his briefing
on Wednesday, but instead,

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:48.434
he chose to brag about this --

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:49.969
-Did you know I was number one
on Facebook?

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:52.204
I mean, I just found out
I'm number one on Facebook.

00:02:52.204 --> 00:02:53.439
I thought that was very nice.

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:56.109
-What the [bleep] are you
talking about, man?

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:57.877
You're in the middle
of a deadly pandemic,

00:02:57.877 --> 00:03:00.546
and you're bragging about
how popular you are on Facebook?

00:03:00.546 --> 00:03:03.782
First of all, of course
you're popular on Facebook.

00:03:03.782 --> 00:03:05.718
It's the preferred method
of communication

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:08.521
of drunk aunts and people
who still own flip phones.

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:10.522
Being number one on Facebook
is like, I don't know,

00:03:10.522 --> 00:03:13.292
having the #1 album in Belgium.

00:03:13.292 --> 00:03:15.227
I mean, good for you, I guess.

00:03:15.227 --> 00:03:17.230
But your album probably sucks.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:18.831
And by the way,
that's not even true.

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:21.668
You only have 28 million
followers on Facebook.

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:23.936
Barack Obama has 53 million.

00:03:23.936 --> 00:03:26.005
I wish someone would point
that out to Trump

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:28.007
because it would annoy the hell
out of him.

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:31.210
He'd force the CDC to update
its coronavirus guidelines.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:34.447
One, stay home.
Two, wash your hands.

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:36.282
Three, follow Donald Trump
on Facebook,

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:38.184
but stay six feet away
from Barack Obama.

00:03:38.184 --> 00:03:41.687
[ As Trump ] We've heard he's
Facebook friends with Tom Hanks.

00:03:41.687 --> 00:03:44.390
So his page definitely,
definitely has it now.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:46.359
[ Normal voice ] The fate
we're currently enduring

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:49.728
and the months of hardship ahead
were not inevitable.

00:03:49.728 --> 00:03:51.764
Hundreds of thousands
of people dying,

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:54.534
a national lockdown that
has disrupted daily life --

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:55.768
None of that had to happen.

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:57.837
I mean, just look at countries
that managed

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:59.739
to successfully contain
the crisis --

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:02.742
Countries much closer to China,
the source of the outbreak,

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:04.010
like Taiwan.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:07.279
-Taiwan is just off the coast
of mainland China.

00:04:07.279 --> 00:04:11.117
Millions travel between Taiwan
and the Chinese mainland.

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:14.487
Johns Hopkins University
had predicted that Taiwan

00:04:14.487 --> 00:04:17.890
would have the second-most
COVID-19 cases in the world.

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:21.126
But today, there are 80
countries and territories

00:04:21.126 --> 00:04:24.797
with more than
Taiwan's 329 cases.

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:27.833
-Taiwan has succeeded at
containing COVID-19

00:04:27.833 --> 00:04:29.268
starting at arrival.

00:04:29.268 --> 00:04:33.139
The first step Taiwan took
was identifying possible cases.

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:36.642
Lee told authorities she'd had
a cough in the last two weeks.

00:04:36.642 --> 00:04:39.412
So security escorted her
to secondary screening.

00:04:39.412 --> 00:04:41.647
She had her temperature taken
like this woman,

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:44.517
and she got a COVID-19 test
at the airport.

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:46.318
Taiwan uploads these results

00:04:46.318 --> 00:04:48.488
into its national
healthcare database.

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:50.222
After her bags were disinfected,

00:04:50.222 --> 00:04:53.059
her ride home was in
a government provided taxi

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:54.227
by herself.

00:04:54.227 --> 00:04:56.128
One phone app allows
Taiwan residents

00:04:56.128 --> 00:04:58.798
to find stores
with masks in stock.

00:04:58.798 --> 00:05:01.099
Another app provides information
on all of those

00:05:01.099 --> 00:05:03.368
who are COVID-19 positive,
where they've been,

00:05:03.368 --> 00:05:04.804
and their case histories.

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:07.440
-Holy [bleep]
They take your temperature,

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.708
give you a test,
disinfect your bags,

00:05:09.708 --> 00:05:10.877
give you a ride home,

00:05:10.877 --> 00:05:12.778
an app that tells you
where to buy masks,

00:05:12.778 --> 00:05:15.481
and you get six months
of Showtime free of charge.

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:16.916
Quarantine yourself
and don't come out

00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:18.818
until you've watched
every episode of "Shameless."

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:21.020
That's certainly better than
what our government is doing.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:24.022
Compare that to when you arrive
at an airport in the U.S.

00:05:24.022 --> 00:05:26.158
The closest anyone comes
to taking your temperature

00:05:26.158 --> 00:05:28.694
is when a TSA agent gives you
a full cavity search

00:05:28.694 --> 00:05:30.963
because you accidentally
packed a bottle of shampoo

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:33.099
that was larger than 3.4 ounces.

00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:36.102
Or if you don't want to look
at Taiwan,

00:05:36.102 --> 00:05:39.605
take Iceland, another country
that's using advanced strategies

00:05:39.605 --> 00:05:41.907
to track and isolate cases
of coronavirus,

00:05:41.907 --> 00:05:44.277
including detective work.

00:05:44.277 --> 00:05:47.179
-For the past few weeks,
Detective Gestur Palmason

00:05:47.179 --> 00:05:50.649
has been chasing down leads
and pursuing suspects.

00:05:50.649 --> 00:05:52.985
He's on the hunt for COVID-19,

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:55.020
where he and dozens
of other detectives

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:59.058
are tracking every single case
of coronavirus in the country.

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:01.761
-As quickly as we can,
we have to reach everyone

00:06:01.761 --> 00:06:04.163
that might have been in contact
with someone who's positive

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:07.899
and try to stop them before they
get in contact with more people.

00:06:07.899 --> 00:06:11.537
-They literally have detectives
tracking down cases.

00:06:11.537 --> 00:06:13.239
Not only is that
an effective method

00:06:13.239 --> 00:06:14.440
for containing the disease,

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:17.242
it's also a great premise
for a Netflix crime drama

00:06:17.242 --> 00:06:20.946
starring Kenneth Branagh
as Detective Gestur Palmason.

00:06:20.946 --> 00:06:23.449
Hey, Kenneth, so excited to be
working with you.

00:06:23.449 --> 00:06:25.551
Have you worked on
an Icelandic accent?

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:27.620
[ British accent ] I think I'll
just use my British accent.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.455
[ Normal voice ] Yeah, but,
no, it takes place in Iceland,

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:31.390
so everyone will have
an Icelandic accent.

00:06:31.390 --> 00:06:32.792
[ British accent ]
No, I think everyone else

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:34.193
should be British, too.

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:36.362
[ Normal voice ] Yeah, but
Kenneth, won't that be weird?

00:06:36.362 --> 00:06:37.396
[ British accent ]
I'm sorry, friend.

00:06:37.396 --> 00:06:39.865
Those are the Kenny Branagh
rules.

00:06:39.865 --> 00:06:42.034
[ Normal voice ]
And that was an extended bit

00:06:42.034 --> 00:06:44.537
for people who have seen
BBC's production

00:06:44.537 --> 00:06:48.006
of the Swedish crime drama
"Wallander."

00:06:48.006 --> 00:06:49.341
Hey, the attic shows
are going to have

00:06:49.341 --> 00:06:51.143
some deep cuts, everybody.

00:06:51.143 --> 00:06:53.612
Thems the rules.

00:06:53.612 --> 00:06:56.148
One of the biggest takeaways
of Iceland's approach

00:06:56.148 --> 00:06:58.283
is that by aggressively testing
everyone,

00:06:58.283 --> 00:06:59.952
they've been able to avoid
having to lock down

00:06:59.952 --> 00:07:01.820
their entire country
the way we've had to.

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:05.190
-It's very important to test
very aggressively.

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:09.562
We put those who test positive
in isolation.

00:07:09.562 --> 00:07:12.931
And we do contact tracing
very aggressively, also.

00:07:12.931 --> 00:07:16.335
We put all contacts
in quarantine.

00:07:16.335 --> 00:07:18.804
And it's interesting that
more than half of those

00:07:18.804 --> 00:07:23.141
who we are diagnosing now
are actually in quarantine

00:07:23.141 --> 00:07:26.446
when they're diagnosed,
which means that our policy

00:07:26.446 --> 00:07:29.148
of quarantine is probably
very effective

00:07:29.148 --> 00:07:31.750
in minimizing the epidemic.

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:34.887
-This has allowed authorities
here to delay the closure

00:07:34.887 --> 00:07:37.823
of bars and restaurants like
in many other major cities.

00:07:37.823 --> 00:07:39.758
Some stores remain open.

00:07:39.758 --> 00:07:43.996
People still walk the streets
and explore the great outdoors.

00:07:43.996 --> 00:07:46.131
-They still get to go outside.

00:07:46.131 --> 00:07:48.067
And their outside is awesome.

00:07:48.067 --> 00:07:50.169
They have lagoons and volcanoes.

00:07:50.169 --> 00:07:52.871
The closest thing we have
to a lagoon here in the U.S.

00:07:52.871 --> 00:07:55.808
is Disney's Typhoon Lagoon,
and that thing is germ city.

00:07:55.808 --> 00:07:58.644
They should call it
Typhoid Lagoon.

00:07:58.644 --> 00:08:00.045
So in Iceland,
they get to go outside.

00:08:00.045 --> 00:08:01.747
Meanwhile, in New York,
to go outside,

00:08:01.747 --> 00:08:03.282
you have to wrap your head
in scarves

00:08:03.282 --> 00:08:06.519
and swerve into the street
to keep a distance of six feet

00:08:06.519 --> 00:08:07.820
from people on the sidewalk.

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:10.589
At this point, you're better off
just hitching a ride

00:08:10.589 --> 00:08:12.257
on the back of a garbage truck.

00:08:12.257 --> 00:08:14.794
New Yorkers aren't used
to avoiding people.

00:08:14.794 --> 00:08:16.161
They're used to bumping into
people.

00:08:16.161 --> 00:08:17.896
That's why the line
in "Midnight Cowboy"

00:08:17.896 --> 00:08:19.565
was, "Hey, I'm walking here!"

00:08:19.565 --> 00:08:21.400
not, "Hey,
I'm trying to maintain

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:23.736
a safe distance of at least
six feet here!"

00:08:23.736 --> 00:08:25.605
And then there's South Korea,

00:08:25.605 --> 00:08:28.407
which had its first case
on the exact same day

00:08:28.407 --> 00:08:30.175
that we had our first case.

00:08:30.175 --> 00:08:32.577
They deployed massive
nationwide testing

00:08:32.577 --> 00:08:34.747
to track and contain
the spread of the disease.

00:08:34.747 --> 00:08:37.049
As Fox News found out
on Wednesday,

00:08:37.049 --> 00:08:39.852
when they invited a doctor on
who was much more critical

00:08:39.852 --> 00:08:42.988
of the Trump administration than
they were probably expecting.

00:08:42.988 --> 00:08:45.558
-Now, what we hear every night
is that the tests,

00:08:45.558 --> 00:08:47.392
that there are millions of tests
available.

00:08:47.392 --> 00:08:52.298
And yet, we don't have that
pinprick blood test you can get,

00:08:52.298 --> 00:08:54.866
you know, at your local doctor
and know in 15 minutes.

00:08:54.866 --> 00:08:56.535
But they're working on it.

00:08:56.535 --> 00:08:58.937
-Yeah, they're working on it.

00:08:58.937 --> 00:09:00.739
They should have been working
on it for months.

00:09:00.739 --> 00:09:03.342
So the fact is we knew about
this from the WHO when?

00:09:03.342 --> 00:09:05.611
December 31st, 2019.

00:09:05.611 --> 00:09:07.512
So last year,
we knew about this.

00:09:07.512 --> 00:09:09.215
We needed this months ago.

00:09:09.215 --> 00:09:11.984
You look at Korea, Korea --
South Korea and the U.S.

00:09:11.984 --> 00:09:14.086
had their first official
confirmed case

00:09:14.086 --> 00:09:17.122
on the same date --
January 19th.

00:09:17.122 --> 00:09:18.790
Let me say this --
January 19th.

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:20.526
You look at what South Korea did
and what we did.

00:09:20.526 --> 00:09:22.494
Their population
is 1/6 of ours.

00:09:22.494 --> 00:09:25.264
Look at the cases they have.
Look at the mortality they have.

00:09:25.264 --> 00:09:28.133
It's a trifle compared to what
we're dealing with right now.

00:09:28.133 --> 00:09:30.769
Because we've had a very weak
response

00:09:30.769 --> 00:09:33.305
and they had a really strong
response.

00:09:33.305 --> 00:09:37.043
-Oh, man. Fox news viewers never
hear that kind of real talk.

00:09:37.043 --> 00:09:38.944
You asked the wrong doctor.

00:09:38.944 --> 00:09:41.647
That's like asking your
weird Uncle if Santa's real.

00:09:41.647 --> 00:09:44.149
[ Inhales sharply ]
Not only is he not real,

00:09:44.149 --> 00:09:46.886
he's just a construct
of a consumeristic system

00:09:46.886 --> 00:09:48.120
designed to melt your brains

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:49.921
before you learn to think
for yourself.

00:09:49.921 --> 00:09:53.458
Anyway -- ho, ho, ho.

00:09:53.458 --> 00:09:56.194
I got you some scratchers.

00:09:56.194 --> 00:09:57.929
Also, I love how long
he shakes his head

00:09:57.929 --> 00:09:59.732
while she's repeating
Trump's talking points.

00:09:59.732 --> 00:10:01.500
They should put that guy
in a box on the screen

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:03.102
during all of Trump's
press briefings.

00:10:03.102 --> 00:10:05.671
-This is a flu.
This is like a flu.

00:10:05.671 --> 00:10:07.673
-So South Korea's
contained the outbreak

00:10:07.673 --> 00:10:08.874
with aggressive testing.

00:10:08.874 --> 00:10:10.742
Meanwhile, here in the U.S.,

00:10:10.742 --> 00:10:13.746
our president said in a
conference call with governors,

00:10:13.746 --> 00:10:16.982
he hadn't even heard about
problems with testing.

00:10:16.982 --> 00:10:19.852
-Do you have any system
in place that you feel

00:10:19.852 --> 00:10:24.490
can adequately identify cases
and isolate them

00:10:24.490 --> 00:10:26.325
and contact trace them?

00:10:26.325 --> 00:10:29.261
Are there capabilities
and resources there

00:10:29.261 --> 00:10:34.299
that's not something you can
do given with what you have?

00:10:34.299 --> 00:10:37.502
-Dr. Fauci, we are trying to do
contact tracing.

00:10:37.502 --> 00:10:40.505
But literally,
we are one day away

00:10:40.505 --> 00:10:43.542
if we don't get test kits
from the CDC

00:10:43.542 --> 00:10:46.011
that we wouldn't be able
to do testing in Montana.

00:10:46.011 --> 00:10:49.715
We just don't have enough
supplies to do the testing.

00:10:49.715 --> 00:10:52.251
-Tony, you can answer
if you want,

00:10:52.251 --> 00:10:54.220
but I haven't heard about
testing in weeks.

00:10:54.220 --> 00:10:56.388
I haven't heard about testing
being a problem.

00:10:56.388 --> 00:10:59.591
-If you haven't heard about
testing being a problem,

00:10:59.591 --> 00:11:02.694
then you need to get tested
to see if you have a problem

00:11:02.694 --> 00:11:05.498
like a hearing test
or a vision test.

00:11:05.498 --> 00:11:08.734
I mean, maybe Trump just can't
read his briefings. Look at him.

00:11:08.734 --> 00:11:10.169
Whenever he reads off
a teleprompter,

00:11:10.169 --> 00:11:14.072
he looks like he just finished
15 rounds with Apollo Creed.

00:11:14.072 --> 00:11:15.640
And now that we've failed
at testing,

00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:18.377
we have to massively ramp up
hospital capacity,

00:11:18.377 --> 00:11:20.112
something the Trump
administration

00:11:20.112 --> 00:11:22.214
is also failing at.

00:11:22.214 --> 00:11:24.149
For example,
hospitals desperately need

00:11:24.149 --> 00:11:25.684
life-saving ventilators.

00:11:25.684 --> 00:11:28.754
And yet the president doesn't
even know what they're called.

00:11:28.754 --> 00:11:32.024
-We sent thousands of generators
to New York.

00:11:32.024 --> 00:11:35.494
The people in New York never
distributed the generators.

00:11:35.494 --> 00:11:38.830
-Ventilators!
They're called ventilators!

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:41.266
Having this guy in charge
is like sending your grandpa

00:11:41.266 --> 00:11:43.135
to GameStop to pick up
video games.

00:11:43.135 --> 00:11:44.970
[ Elderly voice ]
I need the new Line of Duty

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:46.939
for the X-Station Play-Box.

00:11:46.939 --> 00:11:48.740
[ Normal voice ] Also,
now is not the time

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:50.909
to send your grandpa
to GameStop, you coward.

00:11:50.909 --> 00:11:53.845
Just go, grandpa.
You'll be safe.

00:11:53.845 --> 00:11:55.747
Trump doesn't even know
what ventilators are called.

00:11:55.747 --> 00:11:57.582
[ As Trump ] Here are
the emergency ventriloquists

00:11:57.582 --> 00:11:58.884
you guys asked for.

00:11:58.884 --> 00:12:00.752
[ Normal voice ] Oh, actually,
we said ventilators.

00:12:00.752 --> 00:12:03.022
[ As Trump ] I told you he said
ventilators, you dummy.

00:12:03.022 --> 00:12:04.122
[ High-pitched ]
"I'm not the dummy.

00:12:04.122 --> 00:12:05.224
You're the dummy!

00:12:05.224 --> 00:12:10.829
[ Lower-pitched ] Why, I oughta!

00:12:10.829 --> 00:12:12.565
[ Normal voice ] Now, Trump
should have used his powers

00:12:12.565 --> 00:12:14.133
under the Defense Production Act

00:12:14.133 --> 00:12:16.602
to order companies
to make ventilators weeks ago,

00:12:16.602 --> 00:12:19.271
but he's only done it once
during this pandemic,

00:12:19.271 --> 00:12:20.505
even though his administration

00:12:20.505 --> 00:12:23.375
has apparently used it
repeatedly before this.

00:12:23.375 --> 00:12:26.045
"The New York Times" reported
that the Defense Production Act

00:12:26.045 --> 00:12:28.714
has been invoked
hundreds of thousands of times

00:12:28.714 --> 00:12:29.915
in the Trump years.

00:12:29.915 --> 00:12:31.850
But with the pandemic,
the president sees it

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:33.619
as a "Break the Glass"
last resort.

00:12:33.619 --> 00:12:36.521
Hey, man.
It's time to break the glass.

00:12:36.521 --> 00:12:38.523
It was time to break the glass
weeks ago.

00:12:38.523 --> 00:12:40.425
Of course, knowing Trump,
if he does have one of those

00:12:40.425 --> 00:12:42.594
"Break glass in case
of emergency" boxes

00:12:42.594 --> 00:12:44.530
in the White House, it's
probably not a fire alarm,

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:46.931
But, you know, like an emergency
chicken wing.

00:12:46.931 --> 00:12:48.968
And they probably have hundreds
of them on the wall

00:12:48.968 --> 00:12:50.435
because he breaks one
every five minutes.

00:12:50.435 --> 00:12:54.773
Sir, if you want a chicken wing,
you can order it from the chef.

00:12:54.773 --> 00:12:58.510
[ As Trump ] I didn't have time.
It was an emergency.

00:12:58.510 --> 00:13:00.579
[ Normal voice ]
So now we have a situation

00:13:00.579 --> 00:13:03.048
where states are begging
for life-saving ventilators,

00:13:03.048 --> 00:13:05.517
and the Trump team
is in disarray.

00:13:05.517 --> 00:13:08.220
The Pentagon says it still
hasn't sent ventilators

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:10.755
because it hasn't been told
where to send them.

00:13:10.755 --> 00:13:12.424
And the "New York Times"
reported

00:13:12.424 --> 00:13:15.961
that thousands of ventilators
in the stockpile don't work

00:13:15.961 --> 00:13:18.163
because the government
let the contract

00:13:18.163 --> 00:13:21.332
to maintain the stockpile
lapse last summer.

00:13:21.332 --> 00:13:23.635
So now governors are literally
outbidding each other

00:13:23.635 --> 00:13:26.271
on the open market and dealing
with shady middlemen

00:13:26.271 --> 00:13:28.374
and price gouging to buy
ventilators

00:13:28.374 --> 00:13:29.374
wherever they can get them.

00:13:29.374 --> 00:13:31.910
-Every state
does its own purchasing.

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:35.514
So New York is purchasing.
California's purchasing.

00:13:35.514 --> 00:13:36.748
Illinois is purchasing.

00:13:36.748 --> 00:13:39.184
We're all trying to buy
the same commodity --

00:13:39.184 --> 00:13:42.054
Literally the same exact item.

00:13:42.054 --> 00:13:47.126
So you have 50 states competing
to buy the same item.

00:13:47.126 --> 00:13:51.330
We all wind up
bidding up each other

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:53.632
and competing against each other

00:13:53.632 --> 00:13:56.268
where you now literally
will have a company

00:13:56.268 --> 00:13:59.438
call you up and say, "Well,
California just outbid you."

00:13:59.438 --> 00:14:01.406
It's like being on eBay

00:14:01.406 --> 00:14:05.944
with 50 other states
bidding on a ventilator.

00:14:05.944 --> 00:14:08.180
-It's the Wild West.

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:12.551
And these are crazy markets,
and you get a lot of bad actors.

00:14:12.551 --> 00:14:15.353
-It's more like surge pricing
on Uber,

00:14:15.353 --> 00:14:17.690
only at the last moment,
the car drives away

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:19.224
because somebody has outbid you.

00:14:19.224 --> 00:14:21.160
-That's right.
Governors are comparing

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:24.896
buying life-saving ventilators
for a pandemic to surge pricing.

00:14:24.896 --> 00:14:27.099
This is capitalism
at its absolute worst.

00:14:27.099 --> 00:14:29.168
While Trump waits for the market
to decide,

00:14:29.168 --> 00:14:30.735
people are literally
going to die

00:14:30.735 --> 00:14:32.338
and states are getting
ripped off.

00:14:32.338 --> 00:14:35.540
Like they're frying to call
an Uber in the rain in Midtown

00:14:35.540 --> 00:14:37.075
after a Broadway show.

00:14:37.075 --> 00:14:39.611
And even worse, the ventilators
come with a driver

00:14:39.611 --> 00:14:41.079
who won't stop trying to make
a conversation

00:14:41.079 --> 00:14:44.282
even though you're very clearly
trying to take a nap.

00:14:44.282 --> 00:14:47.953
And you'll never guess who's in
charge of this [bleep] show --

00:14:47.953 --> 00:14:50.555
The guy Slender Man
has nightmares about --

00:14:50.555 --> 00:14:51.957
Jared Kushner.

00:14:51.957 --> 00:14:54.693
That's right. The real Slim
Shady has been put in charge

00:14:54.693 --> 00:14:56.128
of the ventilator problem.

00:14:56.128 --> 00:14:58.664
And after New York Governor
Andrew Cuomo said publicly

00:14:58.664 --> 00:15:01.299
that his state needed 30,000
more ventilators,

00:15:01.299 --> 00:15:03.735
apparently Kushner pushed back.

00:15:03.735 --> 00:15:06.271
Kushner told people that Cuomo
is being an alarmist.

00:15:06.271 --> 00:15:08.740
"I have all this this data
about ICU capacity.

00:15:08.740 --> 00:15:10.242
I'm doing my own projections,

00:15:10.242 --> 00:15:12.244
and I've gotten a lot smarter
about this.

00:15:12.244 --> 00:15:14.480
New York doesn't need
all the ventilators.

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:17.282
Oh, oh, you're doing
your own projections?

00:15:17.282 --> 00:15:20.352
Did your parents just buy you
a TI-84?

00:15:20.352 --> 00:15:21.920
You're not qualified
to do anything,

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:25.090
let alone tell New York
how many ventilators they need.

00:15:25.090 --> 00:15:26.491
You're a nepotism case,

00:15:26.491 --> 00:15:28.761
and you only got
the White House job

00:15:28.761 --> 00:15:30.462
because you married
into the family

00:15:30.462 --> 00:15:34.066
and because the security guards
believed your fake I.D.

00:15:34.066 --> 00:15:36.435
"You are good to go, Mr. Cowboy.

00:15:36.435 --> 00:15:39.605
And, hey, give that virus
hell for us."

00:15:39.605 --> 00:15:41.940
I hope when the time
for accountability comes,

00:15:41.940 --> 00:15:44.576
we can all remember that it
didn't have to be like this.

00:15:44.576 --> 00:15:48.380
Other countries responded
to this pandemic with competence

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:49.681
and they avoided the worst.

00:15:49.681 --> 00:15:52.851
Now we're bracing for
an unimaginable tragedy.

00:15:52.851 --> 00:15:55.520
And as we speak, the president
is leaving besieged states

00:15:55.520 --> 00:15:57.222
and hospitals to fend
for themselves,

00:15:57.222 --> 00:16:00.626
putting lives at risk.
But hey, at least...

00:16:00.626 --> 00:16:03.462
-Most people have scarves.
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:16:03.462 --> 00:16:06.498
♪♪

00:16:08.033 --> 00:16:10.369
Stay safe. Wash your hands.
We love you.

